  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1407.02 Requirements for Used Oil Transporters",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1407.02 Requirements for Used Oil Transporters. Used oil transporters shall comply with the requirements of Env-Hw 1405 and, as applicable:\n\n(a) Env-Hw 1407.03 through Env-Hw 1407.09;\n\n(b) Env-Hw 602, Env-Hw 609, and Env-Hw 610 for hazardous waste transporter registration and notification;\n\n(c) Env-Hw 603.02, Env-Hw 603.03, Env-Hw 603.05, Env-Hw 603.07, and Env-Hw 603.08 for vehicle identification, security, and safety;\n\n(d) US DOT regulations in 49 CFR parts 171 through 180;\n\n(e) Rules adopted by the New Hampshire department of safety;\n\n(f) Env-Hw 1406 for generating used oil;\n\n(g) Env-Hw 1408 for processing or re-refining used oil, except as provided under Env-Hw 1407.03;\n\n(h) Env-Hw 1409 for burning used oil for energy recovery; and\n\n(i) Env-Hw 1410 for acting as a used oil fuel marketer.\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
